-- title:
--   Row-10 Newton residual polynomial coefficients
-- statement:
--   These are explicit finite coefficient data for the degree-10 inverse cubic of a fifth power of $z^3-z-\beta$. The algebraic parameter used in the later proofs satisfies $\alpha^3=1001/20-66\alpha+21\alpha^2$. The bundle defines the explicit degree-at-most-61 polynomial
--   $$E_\alpha(t)=\sum_{j=0}^{61}e_j(\alpha)t^j.$$
--   Each coefficient is a rational quadratic expression in $\alpha$. This is the residual polynomial used in the separately verified identity $G(t,P_\alpha(t))=t^{32}E_\alpha(t)$. Keeping the residual coefficients in their own file permits independent caching and verification.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

